{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:d6c21784fd20c6b2","name":"Sandstorm","source":{"id":"source:reference-d6c21784fd20c6b2","title":"Sandstorm","revision":21432,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:47:28Z","sha256":"d9e4f53b7826d755d697121e45f361ebd2ef3e88a00d55055dc62ad696d13ae6","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21432","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Sandstorm&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-d6c21784fd20c6b2","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["The sand whips past you at blinding speed, eroding any exposed objects or flesh."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Creatures caught in the middle of a Sandstorm face a number of problems. Aside from the large volume of sand blowing across open surfaces and bare flesh at high speeds, the storm hinders vision. Enemies several meters away who could be seen clearly under normal conditions can barely be seen during a Sandstorm, if at all. A Sandstorm can be a challenging place for combat- or it can present a chance for creatures to make their escape from foes.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Sandstorm Statistics (CL 4)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Keywords:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Area"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Area"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Atmosphere"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Atmosphere"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Natural"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Natural"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trigger:"]}," A being begins its turn in the Sandstorm.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Attack:"]}," +6 vs ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 2d10+1 (Half Damage on Miss)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Recurrence:"]}," Hourly, until the being leaves the Sandstorm.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"},":"]}," The following are suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"}," for this Hazard:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knowledge (Physical Sciences)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knowledge_(Physical_Sciences)"}," (DC 21):"]}," The character determines that the incoming cloud is a violent Sandstorm, and all members of the group gain a +1 circumstance bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"}," against the Hazard."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," (DC 16):"]}," The character detects the Sandstorm before it reaches them."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," A Sandstorm grants ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concealment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concealment"}," to beings and objects within it. Any target wearing a sealed protective suit is not affected by this Hazard.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
